WEBVTT

00:00:04.540 --> 00:00:06.410
A well storm?

00:00:06.410 --> 00:00:09.250
Because I remembered who I am?

00:00:09.250 --> 00:00:13.290
Which means, this id well is mine!

00:00:13.290 --> 00:00:16.870
Which also means, in the end...

00:00:16.870 --> 00:00:19.700
...John Walker was manipulating me, too!

00:01:58.910 --> 00:02:00.540
Well storm expanding!

00:02:00.540 --> 00:02:02.950
The well itself also continues to expand!

00:02:02.950 --> 00:02:07.580
We've completely lost Sakaido's position!
We can't track him!

00:02:07.580 --> 00:02:09.410
Cut the Mizuhanome's power!

00:02:09.410 --> 00:02:10.870
That's without precedent!

00:02:10.870 --> 00:02:14.910
Formation of a well storm is
without precedent. Just do it!

00:02:18.290 --> 00:02:20.290
I can't! There's no response!

00:02:20.290 --> 00:02:23.580
The Mizuhanome is protecting the well.

00:02:25.450 --> 00:02:28.080
This well wasn't from the Kura's repository.

00:02:28.080 --> 00:02:32.700
It was created from cognition particles
gleaned at Momoki's home.

00:02:32.700 --> 00:02:35.290
That rules out a mix-up
or switcheroo at the Kura.

00:02:35.290 --> 00:02:39.330
And the Wakumusubi-Mizuhanome link
wouldn't allow such a thing.

00:02:39.330 --> 00:02:42.500
Which means, the switch happened at the scene.

00:02:42.500 --> 00:02:48.870
Either Mr. Matsuoka set a trap,
or he fell into one set by someone else.

00:02:48.870 --> 00:02:51.540
Investigate Field Analyst Matsuoka's movements.

00:02:51.540 --> 00:02:52.370
Yes, ma'am.

00:02:52.370 --> 00:02:54.200
--I'm already on it.
--What?

00:02:54.200 --> 00:02:58.450
When you're thinking,
you neglect everything else.

00:02:59.790 --> 00:03:01.080
Nice backup!

00:03:01.080 --> 00:03:03.910
What are you so proud of?

00:03:03.910 --> 00:03:05.200
Got it.

00:03:05.200 --> 00:03:07.950
Between entering the bedroom
and the Wakumusubi scan,

00:03:07.950 --> 00:03:11.250
Matsuoka did nothing suspicious.

00:03:11.250 --> 00:03:14.830
Check whether any other investigators
entered the bedroom.

00:03:14.830 --> 00:03:15.660
Yes, ma'am.

00:03:15.660 --> 00:03:18.620
Connect me to Mr. Matsuoka.

00:03:18.620 --> 00:03:21.370
Okay. Returning to the scene.

00:03:21.370 --> 00:03:24.910
Whoever did this, I don't appreciate
being taken for a ride!

00:03:31.580 --> 00:03:33.950
Why'd you do it?

00:03:35.540 --> 00:03:37.540
What's your game?

00:03:39.620 --> 00:03:41.410
Say something!

00:03:45.660 --> 00:03:47.370
What's wrong?

00:03:47.370 --> 00:03:50.330
Why are you going to let me kill you?

00:03:50.330 --> 00:03:53.580
Don't I deserve it for what I did?

00:03:53.580 --> 00:03:58.750
I purposely trapped you in this well--
after dreaming of this situation.

00:03:58.750 --> 00:04:02.160
When the opportunity arose,
something drove me forward,

00:04:02.160 --> 00:04:08.080
so I went with it--knowing full well
what it would mean.

00:04:09.540 --> 00:04:14.330
Come on. Take it out on me.

00:04:14.330 --> 00:04:16.290
No.

00:04:16.290 --> 00:04:18.500
I reject your little offer.

00:04:21.410 --> 00:04:23.540
I need to think!

00:04:23.540 --> 00:04:25.410
You think, too!

00:04:25.410 --> 00:04:30.700
Surrendering to rage and beating you to death
would play into John Walker's hands.

00:04:30.700 --> 00:04:34.500
John Walker wants me to kill you.

00:04:34.500 --> 00:04:38.120
It's a problem for him if you're still around.

00:04:39.200 --> 00:04:40.910
Why?

00:04:40.910 --> 00:04:43.950
Why'd you go along with that?

00:04:43.950 --> 00:04:45.160
Of course.

00:04:45.160 --> 00:04:47.120
You <i>want </i>to die.

00:04:47.120 --> 00:04:48.040
Why?

00:04:48.040 --> 00:04:50.040
What could be so unbearable?

00:04:50.040 --> 00:04:54.040
You even survived drilling a hole in your head.

00:04:54.040 --> 00:04:58.500
Wait, why <i>did </i>you drill a hole in your head?

00:04:58.500 --> 00:05:01.040
What was so awful back then?

00:05:01.040 --> 00:05:03.910
As a brilliant detective who's missing the hole,

00:05:03.910 --> 00:05:06.200
what's so awful now?

00:05:07.750 --> 00:05:09.370
Hey.

00:05:09.370 --> 00:05:11.580
What are you looking at?

00:05:15.500 --> 00:05:17.750
The numbers?

00:05:17.750 --> 00:05:19.700
Hey, what's all this?

00:05:19.700 --> 00:05:21.660
I was bored.

00:05:21.660 --> 00:05:24.120
I was counting sand.

00:05:26.080 --> 00:05:28.160
Who're you?

00:05:29.200 --> 00:05:30.410
Who are <i>you</i>?

00:05:30.410 --> 00:05:32.120
Wow. How cool.

00:05:32.120 --> 00:05:34.950
Wow. That's harsh, but you're exactly right.

00:05:34.950 --> 00:05:37.040
Don't point at me.

00:05:39.080 --> 00:05:42.080
Your favorite number... It's three, right?

00:05:43.750 --> 00:05:47.450
Guess I'll pass up another
perfect opportunity to die.

00:05:47.450 --> 00:05:50.910
Yeah, three is a nice number.

00:05:50.910 --> 00:05:52.910
It's a wonderful number.

00:05:52.910 --> 00:05:57.790
John Walker needed for you to die.

00:05:57.790 --> 00:06:01.830
That's because once the sand is gone,
this is a world of numbers.

00:06:01.830 --> 00:06:04.160
And you're held captive by numbers.

00:06:04.160 --> 00:06:07.370
You can't help but count them.

00:06:07.370 --> 00:06:11.450
You have arithmomania, don't you?

00:06:11.450 --> 00:06:15.950
You put a drill to you head to
escape the agony of it, didn't you.

00:06:17.750 --> 00:06:20.870
However, becoming a
brilliant detective closed the hole,

00:06:20.870 --> 00:06:24.250
and as a result, your arithmomania returned.

00:06:24.250 --> 00:06:27.580
A brilliant detective's intellect
must make it quite a burden.

00:06:27.580 --> 00:06:29.830
That's why you're trying to die.

00:06:31.830 --> 00:06:33.910
You nailed it.

00:06:33.910 --> 00:06:35.290
I <i>do </i>sympathize.

00:06:35.290 --> 00:06:38.120
But I won't give you the death you seek.

00:06:38.120 --> 00:06:40.250
There's something only you can do.

00:06:40.250 --> 00:06:42.830
That John Walker doesn't want you to do.

00:06:42.830 --> 00:06:44.580
A job I need you to do.

00:06:45.830 --> 00:06:48.120
Are you kidding me?

00:06:48.120 --> 00:06:50.660
But I'm intrigued.

00:06:50.660 --> 00:06:52.750
What's the job?

00:06:52.750 --> 00:06:57.660
Have you noticed? The cockpit
was just right here, but it's gone.

00:06:58.790 --> 00:07:00.290
It was huge. How could...

00:07:00.290 --> 00:07:03.950
You entered my other well, right?

00:07:03.950 --> 00:07:08.080
It was also a world with lines of numbers.

00:07:08.080 --> 00:07:11.540
And Kaeru was also there,
at the starting point.

00:07:11.540 --> 00:07:15.910
Furthermore, I expect she was
attached dead to your wrist.

00:07:15.910 --> 00:07:17.500
With handcuffs.

00:07:17.500 --> 00:07:21.500
The other you in that world used handcuffs.

00:07:21.500 --> 00:07:22.750
I see.

00:07:22.750 --> 00:07:27.660
Were you able to find the cockpit
Hondomachi was in?

00:07:27.660 --> 00:07:28.870
Yeah.

00:07:28.870 --> 00:07:34.290
I mean, there was no easy way for me
to immediately kill myself in your well.

00:07:34.290 --> 00:07:35.750
It was lightning.

00:07:35.750 --> 00:07:39.790
I had to wait forever for it
to zap me. It was hell.

00:07:39.790 --> 00:07:42.160
Regardless, if you found the cockpit,

00:07:42.160 --> 00:07:47.200
then don't you remember the numbers
on the path you took to reach it?

00:07:48.410 --> 00:07:49.750
Yup.

00:07:51.910 --> 00:07:54.080
Not just the ones on the path.

00:07:54.080 --> 00:07:58.830
I remember every number
that entered my field of vision.

00:08:00.370 --> 00:08:05.750
As long as there are more numbers,
I'm compelled to take them all in, after all.

00:08:06.540 --> 00:08:12.580
Then you can place our position
on the map inside your head.

00:08:12.580 --> 00:08:14.000
I can.

00:08:14.000 --> 00:08:16.540
And what you want to find.

00:08:16.540 --> 00:08:18.290
Will it be there, I wonder.

00:08:19.580 --> 00:08:21.950
The storm is expanding.

00:08:21.950 --> 00:08:27.080
That means the Mizuhanome and this id well
are most likely continuing to update.

00:08:27.080 --> 00:08:31.120
Which must be why the cockpit disappeared.

00:08:31.120 --> 00:08:32.160
Hey, wait.

00:08:32.160 --> 00:08:33.410
Assistant Director Togo!

00:08:33.410 --> 00:08:34.290
Yes?

00:08:34.290 --> 00:08:39.250
I took my eyes off Narihisago's
original well for a moment, and now...

00:08:40.330 --> 00:08:42.200
...the cockpit is gone!

00:08:42.200 --> 00:08:43.080
Kokufu!

00:08:43.080 --> 00:08:45.250
Sorry. Give me a moment.

00:08:46.580 --> 00:08:52.120
The cockpit's disappeared from the lightning
well when the well storm appeared in the desert.

00:08:52.120 --> 00:08:54.160
Keep an eye on the issue.

00:08:55.120 --> 00:08:58.410
I know our brilliant detectives will come back.

00:09:02.200 --> 00:09:07.200
I bet the Mizuhanome's updates
brought her cockpit to our well.

00:09:07.200 --> 00:09:10.370
And most likely Hondomachi along with it.

00:09:10.370 --> 00:09:12.580
But where? This well is huge.

00:09:12.580 --> 00:09:14.000
In the same spot.

00:09:14.000 --> 00:09:16.750
It's the same well at different times.

00:09:16.750 --> 00:09:18.500
Holy hell.

00:09:18.500 --> 00:09:21.910
Why does your well always have to be so brutal?

00:09:21.910 --> 00:09:29.540
But thanks to that, we've gotten rid of
our observers, which gives us a chance.

00:09:30.700 --> 00:09:36.410
Sometimes you sleep for only a short time,
but the dream lasts much much longer.

00:09:36.410 --> 00:09:38.500
You've experienced that, right?

00:09:38.500 --> 00:09:40.040
Why does that matter?

00:09:40.040 --> 00:09:45.160
The same kind of thing happened to me
when I entered the well within this well.

00:09:45.160 --> 00:09:47.040
In those ten minutes?

00:09:47.040 --> 00:09:51.040
I lived in that well for more than a year.

00:09:52.200 --> 00:09:53.120
Incredible!

00:09:53.120 --> 00:09:54.370
Lucky you.

00:09:54.370 --> 00:09:59.450
Yeah, but that's never happened
in a normal id well.

00:09:59.450 --> 00:10:03.790
Time in the well is synchronized
with time in the outside world.

00:10:03.790 --> 00:10:05.580
What was the difference?

00:10:05.580 --> 00:10:08.200
And what did it have in common with dreams?

00:10:08.200 --> 00:10:15.370
Oh, whether someone is observing
the world from the outside, right?

00:10:15.370 --> 00:10:19.200
If there's someone else to observe
the events, time is synced,

00:10:19.200 --> 00:10:22.370
but otherwise, time is free
to dilate or contract.

00:10:22.370 --> 00:10:23.450
I see.

00:10:23.450 --> 00:10:26.700
That's how we have a chance.

00:10:26.700 --> 00:10:29.950
The five minutes we have left
is in the outside world.

00:10:29.950 --> 00:10:34.080
And the same chance is available
in the well within the well.

00:10:34.080 --> 00:10:36.200
To Hondomachi.

00:10:40.750 --> 00:10:42.450
Mr. Narihisago.

00:10:42.450 --> 00:10:47.700
Even though he believed this was reality,
he managed to do all this...

00:10:47.700 --> 00:10:49.370
But be that as it may,

00:10:49.370 --> 00:10:55.580
the serial killers all have their own
preferred means to kill, like a mark.

00:10:55.580 --> 00:10:58.040
The Challenger pummels his victims one-on-one,

00:10:58.040 --> 00:10:59.120
the Face-lifter removes faces,

00:10:59.120 --> 00:11:00.040
removes faces,

00:11:00.040 --> 00:11:02.080
pulls out tongues,

00:11:02.080 --> 00:11:06.500
the Thigh-severer severs both legs,
and the Arm-twister pulls arms apart.

00:11:06.500 --> 00:11:11.620
Whether these preferences come from
roles John Walker forced on them,

00:11:11.620 --> 00:11:17.200
or John Walker merely caused the killers'
own preferences to surface, I can't say.

00:11:17.200 --> 00:11:21.790
Regardless, if I consider the various
serial killers throughout history,

00:11:21.790 --> 00:11:25.830
there's a clear tendency to use
a particular means of killing.

00:11:25.830 --> 00:11:32.790
Which means, John Walker ought to have
his own particular way of doing things, too.

00:11:32.790 --> 00:11:35.290
Narihisago also reached that conclusion.

00:11:39.660 --> 00:11:42.870
And I can see the answer.

00:11:42.870 --> 00:11:44.910
Don't they all die immediately?

00:11:44.910 --> 00:11:49.620
No one dies immediately.
They linger for a while.

00:11:49.620 --> 00:11:51.120
The Perforator.

00:11:52.620 --> 00:11:54.660
It's not just Fukuda Tamotsu.

00:11:54.660 --> 00:12:01.000
The victims of the John Walker's serial killers
don't necessarily die right away.

00:12:01.000 --> 00:12:04.370
The Face-lifter, Thigh-severer,
and Arm-twister...

00:12:04.370 --> 00:12:09.750
In the real world, they had victims get rescued,
which helped lead to their arrest.

00:12:10.120 --> 00:12:14.370
He creates killers whose victims
don't necessarily die.

00:12:14.370 --> 00:12:16.450
That's John Walker's M.O.

00:12:16.450 --> 00:12:18.290
Yeah. That works.

00:12:18.290 --> 00:12:20.700
I need to keep going.

00:12:20.700 --> 00:12:24.870
Let's see... What else do they have in common?

00:12:24.870 --> 00:12:28.790
The maximum number of victims is seven.

00:12:28.790 --> 00:12:32.830
Assuming John Walker works at the Kura...

00:12:32.830 --> 00:12:39.580
Either the victims are found alive,
or the police arrest the killer he created...

00:12:39.580 --> 00:12:43.500
Or... he gets an officer to kill them.

00:12:43.500 --> 00:12:45.660
Never more than seven deaths.

00:12:47.410 --> 00:12:49.450
Seven...

00:12:49.450 --> 00:12:53.410
If the acceleration of John Walker's plans

00:12:53.410 --> 00:13:00.700
by having Director Momoki arrested
is a precursor to him ceasing his activity,

00:13:00.700 --> 00:13:04.250
or moving to new methods...

00:13:04.250 --> 00:13:06.910
Then the number seven also has meaning.

00:13:08.000 --> 00:13:09.660
I knew it.

00:13:09.660 --> 00:13:12.790
The timeline for the victims only appears random

00:13:12.790 --> 00:13:17.000
because it's based on date of
discovery and time of death.

00:13:17.000 --> 00:13:20.750
The dates the victims
actually died are irregular,

00:13:20.750 --> 00:13:24.080
but if you redo it by
the date of the killing blow...

00:13:24.080 --> 00:13:25.950
Everything lines up.

00:13:25.950 --> 00:13:28.120
Thigh-severer on Mondays,

00:13:28.120 --> 00:13:29.830
Face-lifter on Tuesdays,

00:13:29.830 --> 00:13:31.450
Tongue-tearer on Wednesdays,

00:13:31.450 --> 00:13:33.290
Gravedigger on Thursdays,

00:13:33.290 --> 00:13:35.120
Arm-twister on Fridays,

00:13:35.120 --> 00:13:37.250
Perforator on Saturdays...

00:13:37.250 --> 00:13:40.040
Come to think of it,

00:13:40.040 --> 00:13:43.450
the day Oonuki Yuji was killed and
I was injured was also a Saturday, huh.

00:13:43.450 --> 00:13:49.370
And finally, the Challenger's killings and
Narihisago Muku's death were on Sunday.

00:13:49.370 --> 00:13:56.450
John Walker's been manipulating their
drive to kill on particular days of the week.

00:13:56.450 --> 00:13:59.660
Just as if it were his job.

00:13:59.660 --> 00:14:04.450
Or as if... he were God
creating the world in seven days.

00:14:07.540 --> 00:14:10.040
Hey, Hondomachi. Where are you right now?

00:14:10.040 --> 00:14:12.200
Why did you just disappear?

00:14:12.200 --> 00:14:13.370
I'm sorry.

00:14:13.370 --> 00:14:15.330
I had to look into something.

00:14:15.330 --> 00:14:17.080
Next time say something!

00:14:17.080 --> 00:14:20.290
So, what happened with Fukuda Tamotsu?

00:14:20.290 --> 00:14:21.160
Huh?

00:14:21.160 --> 00:14:22.250
He escaped!

00:14:22.250 --> 00:14:24.040
By pretending to be the victim.

00:14:24.040 --> 00:14:25.330
Is that so?

00:14:25.330 --> 00:14:27.290
Sorry, I have to go.

00:14:27.290 --> 00:14:29.250
What? Hey!

00:14:33.290 --> 00:14:34.750
I better hurry.

00:14:35.660 --> 00:14:37.120
We found it!

00:14:37.120 --> 00:14:39.500
And the little lady, too!

00:14:39.500 --> 00:14:41.080
Fukuda Tamotsu.

00:14:41.080 --> 00:14:42.580
Don't move.

00:14:42.580 --> 00:14:45.700
Who're you? How'd you find this place?

00:14:45.700 --> 00:14:49.410
Sorry. I don't have time to explain.

00:14:49.410 --> 00:14:55.700
For reasons you're not aware of,
I know about this place and about you.

00:14:55.700 --> 00:14:57.660
What could you possibly know?

00:14:57.660 --> 00:15:02.830
What you really need to do is run that
drill through your head again, right?

00:15:02.830 --> 00:15:06.750
Since that's what you want more than anything.

00:15:06.750 --> 00:15:10.250
And so I don't really intend to shoot you.

00:15:10.250 --> 00:15:15.290
And you no longer intend
to use that drill on me.

00:15:15.290 --> 00:15:17.750
As for how I could know that,

00:15:17.750 --> 00:15:22.660
it's because I myself once
put a hole in my head,

00:15:22.660 --> 00:15:25.580
with the very drill you're holding now.

00:15:28.410 --> 00:15:30.580
I don't know what you're saying,

00:15:30.580 --> 00:15:35.830
and yet you're right about me,
so you must be telling the truth.

00:15:37.160 --> 00:15:39.620
How did you like your hole?

00:15:39.620 --> 00:15:42.250
Now I can't believe it's gone.

00:15:42.250 --> 00:15:43.750
You took a liking to it?

00:15:43.750 --> 00:15:45.450
More like...

00:15:45.450 --> 00:15:48.540
It was just part of me.

00:15:49.830 --> 00:15:53.700
Who knew you need to lose something
in order to feel complete.

00:15:53.700 --> 00:15:56.080
Yeah.

00:15:56.080 --> 00:15:57.250
So?

00:15:57.250 --> 00:16:00.040
What brings you here?

00:16:00.950 --> 00:16:03.290
I want to know about your dreams.

00:16:04.290 --> 00:16:08.250
Have you seen this person in your dreams?

00:16:08.250 --> 00:16:09.580
Yep.

00:16:09.580 --> 00:16:15.120
On August 15th three years ago,
and September 7th, and September 10th.

00:16:16.200 --> 00:16:18.120
How do you remember so precisely?

00:16:18.120 --> 00:16:21.160
I used to be very good with numbers.

00:16:21.160 --> 00:16:23.370
Not so much now.

00:16:23.370 --> 00:16:25.250
Do you remember the time?

00:16:25.250 --> 00:16:26.370
Yep.

00:16:26.370 --> 00:16:30.000
August 15th was 2 to 3 p.m.

00:16:30.000 --> 00:16:33.370
September 7th was 11 p.m. to 3 a.m.

00:16:33.370 --> 00:16:36.830
September 10th was also 11 p.m. to 3 a.m.

00:16:36.830 --> 00:16:38.870
You wake up early.

00:16:38.870 --> 00:16:40.370
Was the 15th a nap?

00:16:40.370 --> 00:16:45.160
No, no. I drilled the hole in my head
that day, so I collapsed.

00:16:45.160 --> 00:16:49.250
But instead of dying, I saw this old dude.

00:16:49.250 --> 00:16:52.160
Okay. What happened in those dreams?

00:16:52.160 --> 00:16:53.620
Not much.

00:16:53.620 --> 00:16:59.910
There was a girl there, and he invited me
to drill a hole in her head.

00:16:59.910 --> 00:17:02.580
I just told him I wasn't interested.

00:17:02.580 --> 00:17:07.370
The other two days, I had the same dream,
and I turned him down again.

00:17:07.370 --> 00:17:09.870
I said dream holes don't interest me.

00:17:09.870 --> 00:17:13.450
That's not what your holes are about, after all.

00:17:13.450 --> 00:17:14.700
Shoot.

00:17:14.700 --> 00:17:18.410
No one with access to the well data was off duty

00:17:18.410 --> 00:17:22.620
on the afternoon of August 15th three years ago.

00:17:22.620 --> 00:17:23.950
Off duty?

00:17:23.950 --> 00:17:27.000
Couldn't someone have just taken a nap at work?

00:17:27.000 --> 00:17:28.290
A nap?

00:17:28.290 --> 00:17:33.910
Okay, how about someone who took work
seriously but was asleep that afternoon?

00:17:34.910 --> 00:17:39.000
Daytime for us is nighttime for others, right?

00:17:39.000 --> 00:17:41.040
An overseas business trip?

00:17:42.540 --> 00:17:43.870
Are you a cop?

00:17:43.870 --> 00:17:45.290
Yeah.

00:17:45.290 --> 00:17:47.000
Will we get to meet again?

00:17:47.000 --> 00:17:48.120
Dunno.

00:17:48.120 --> 00:17:52.870
But getting caught by the police
will open a new door for you.

00:17:54.000 --> 00:17:56.700
If you say so, I'll believe that.

00:17:58.870 --> 00:18:00.120
I'm here.

00:18:00.120 --> 00:18:02.540
Momoki's bedroom, as instructed.

00:18:02.540 --> 00:18:06.790
Mr. Matsuoka, get me detailed
visual data for everything in the room.

00:18:06.790 --> 00:18:08.660
Roger.

00:18:08.660 --> 00:18:15.040
Are there any traces of something being moved,
or signs something was brought in?

00:18:15.040 --> 00:18:16.160
Huh?

00:18:16.160 --> 00:18:20.500
I've known Momoki a long time,
but I've never been in his room.

00:18:20.500 --> 00:18:23.450
I'll look around, but I can't speak to--

00:18:24.750 --> 00:18:28.750
Mr. Matsuoka, see the picture frame over there?

00:18:30.040 --> 00:18:31.160
This?

00:18:31.160 --> 00:18:32.790
Test it.

00:18:43.080 --> 00:18:46.370
Go back to the bedroom and scan it again.

00:18:46.370 --> 00:18:47.660
Okay.

00:18:51.250 --> 00:18:52.660
You did it, Togo.

00:18:52.660 --> 00:18:54.500
Incredible. How?

00:18:54.500 --> 00:18:57.830
That picture wasn't there when I visited before.

00:19:03.700 --> 00:19:05.500
What's this?

00:19:05.500 --> 00:19:08.200
Of course. It's Narihisago's.

00:19:09.370 --> 00:19:15.660
Cognition particles from when he drove
Fuyukawa to suicide were on this picture.

00:19:15.660 --> 00:19:18.620
Find out who had access to the photo!

00:19:18.620 --> 00:19:23.040
Well, time to wake her up and
surprise her with this desert.

00:19:23.040 --> 00:19:29.660
On August 15th three years ago, a high-ranking
officer went to New York for training.

00:19:29.660 --> 00:19:30.540
Hello?

00:19:30.540 --> 00:19:34.160
Oh, hello? Is this Mr. John Walker?

00:19:38.870 --> 00:19:41.500
Ooh, right on time!

00:19:41.500 --> 00:19:43.450
Bye! And thanks!

00:19:50.790 --> 00:19:52.790
You're welcome.

00:19:57.330 --> 00:20:00.040
Who am I? Where am I?

00:20:00.040 --> 00:20:05.540
You're in the id well of brilliant detective
Sakaido, a.k.a. Narihisago Akihito.

00:20:05.540 --> 00:20:07.330
Hondomachi.

00:20:10.870 --> 00:20:14.450
Nice hole you've got there.

00:20:14.450 --> 00:20:17.250
Well, it's who I am.

00:20:17.250 --> 00:20:19.410
More importantly, what is this?

00:20:19.410 --> 00:20:23.200
After three years, the lightning abated.

00:20:23.200 --> 00:20:24.910
Isn't that great?

00:20:26.000 --> 00:20:27.700
I suppose.

00:20:27.700 --> 00:20:29.870
It's empty now.

00:20:30.950 --> 00:20:32.580
That reminds me.

00:20:32.580 --> 00:20:33.830
Thank you.

00:20:33.830 --> 00:20:34.870
For what?

00:20:34.870 --> 00:20:36.750
Well, not you exactly.

00:20:36.750 --> 00:20:40.750
Mr. Narihisago, I finished the investigation!

00:20:40.750 --> 00:20:43.540
I figured out John Walker's identity!

00:20:43.540 --> 00:20:46.200
It's Chief Hayaseura!

00:20:46.200 --> 00:20:47.620
Is that right.

00:20:48.830 --> 00:20:51.120
Let's head back to Kaeru.

00:20:53.450 --> 00:20:56.790
Why do you think that will save us?

00:20:56.790 --> 00:21:03.750
Kaeru is a victim of murder, and of
this world itself, and we're the detectives.

00:21:03.750 --> 00:21:08.580
We solve her mystery. She would never
harbor ill will towards us, right?

00:21:08.580 --> 00:21:12.160
She told us at the very beginning.
To stay near her.

00:21:12.160 --> 00:21:15.450
Okay. And just who is Kaeru?

00:21:15.450 --> 00:21:18.330
Who's seeking your help?

00:21:21.000 --> 00:21:23.370
Who is Asukai Kiki, exactly?

00:21:23.370 --> 00:21:26.040
Why does she look so much like Kaeru?

00:21:26.040 --> 00:21:29.450
A serial killer comes to your dreams.

00:21:29.450 --> 00:21:31.120
To kill you.

00:21:31.120 --> 00:21:34.290
That's the only kind of person that comes.

00:21:34.290 --> 00:21:37.450
Ms. Asukai's telepathic ability.

00:21:37.450 --> 00:21:40.910
Serial killers' entrance into her dreams.

00:21:40.910 --> 00:21:42.450
Many drives to kill.

00:21:42.450 --> 00:21:44.040
Sorry for calling so late.

00:21:44.040 --> 00:21:47.660
Listen, Ms. Asukai disappeared.

00:21:47.660 --> 00:21:53.620
Narihisago, did Ms. Asukai say
anything to you that might help?

00:21:53.620 --> 00:21:57.370
In fact... she did.

00:21:57.370 --> 00:21:59.910
Togo! The brilliant detectives!

00:22:02.540 --> 00:22:06.540
We had a chance precisely because
they couldn't observe us.

00:22:07.700 --> 00:22:10.830
Time is about to synchronize.

00:22:10.830 --> 00:22:12.250
Extract!

00:22:14.660 --> 00:22:17.250
Koharu, are you all right?

00:22:17.250 --> 00:22:21.950
I'm fine. More importantly,
we know John Walker's identity!

00:22:21.950 --> 00:22:23.870
It's Chief Hayaseura!

00:22:28.080 --> 00:22:30.750
Obtain an arrest warrant! Detain him!

00:22:30.750 --> 00:22:32.580
Contact Metropolitan Police.

00:22:34.290 --> 00:22:36.370
What's going on? Why?

00:22:36.370 --> 00:22:37.540
It's the Mizuhanome!

00:22:37.540 --> 00:22:39.660
Main power has been cut!

00:22:55.660 --> 00:22:59.080
It's as if I put you in here yesterday.

00:23:03.500 --> 00:23:08.000
You're up, Asukai Kiki.
